# packages/orpc

- `routers/public` (no session) and `routers/admin` (all on `adminProcedure`, cookie + `x-csrf-token: orpc`). Admin
  procedures stay in `routers/admin`; the router test fails if one answers a visitor.
- Business rules live in `lib/` (`orders.ts` stock holds and `settleOrder`, `payments.ts` providers, `storage.ts` S3,
  `settings.ts`), routers stay thin.
- Stock is decremented when an order is created and returned on cancel/refund/expiry (`releaseExpiredHolds`, lazy, 45 min).
- Tests: `router.test.ts` runs against a real Postgres (`DATABASE_URL`, skipped without).
